From 7b909338a4a60739db88ac99bd5eac0c420d6d4b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 11:36:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test(delegate): survive a throttled runner when waiting for a
 background completion [daveey]

queue.Queue.get times out on wall clock. A 5s budget expired on CI after the
children had already printed complete, because post-child persist had not yet
published the event. 60s still returns as soon as the event is queued.

Problem: test_nonfinite_marker_preserves_background_dispatch[False-None] failed
with _queue.Empty on the first attempt of run 40846416856 and passed on retry.
Why 1: completion_queue.get(timeout=5) raised Empty (queue.py:209).
Why 2: the event is put only after post-child persist (async_delegation.py),
which had not finished inside 5s of wall clock.
Why 3: Queue.get's deadline is time.time(), so a CPU stall advances it while
the producer is not scheduled. A 6s SIGSTOP during get reproduces Empty; the
same stop passes at 60s.
Root: the assertion's deadline was shorter than the work it waits on under
the runner's CPU quota.
Not caught: the file retry paints pass-on-retry green, so CI stayed green.
---
 tests/tools/test_finite_delegation_outcomes.py | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/tests/tools/test_finite_delegation_outcomes.py b/tests/tools/test_finite_delegation_outcomes.py
index 9fdab078ca..efe5bad180 100644
--- a/tests/tools/test_finite_delegation_outcomes.py
+++ b/tests/tools/test_finite_delegation_outcomes.py
@@ -233,8 +233,12 @@ def test_nonfinite_marker_preserves_background_dispatch(harness, monkeypatch, ma
     assert result["status"] == "dispatched", result
     assert result["mode"] == "background"
     assert "results" not in result
-    event = process_registry.completion_queue.get(timeout=5)
+    # Queue.get times out on wall clock (time.time). A CPU-throttled runner can
+    # burn a 5s budget after the children have already finished, before the
+    # post-child persist publishes the event. 60s still returns as soon as the
+    # event is queued; only a real hang waits it out.
+    event = process_registry.completion_queue.get(timeout=60)
     assert event["type"] == "async_delegation"
     if api_history:
         assert event["origin_session_id"] == "history-session"
-    assert all(child.closed.wait(2) for child in children)
+    assert all(child.closed.wait(60) for child in children)
